1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,790
What if Earth's
core cooled

2
00:00:01,790 --> 00:00:04,860
until it was
completely solid?

3
00:00:04,860 --> 00:00:07,480
Today, only the
center is solid,

4
00:00:07,480 --> 00:00:09,980
as hot as the
Sun's surface.

5
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:13,710
Around it swirls an
ocean of molten iron.

6
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:16,660
That churning
iron is a dynamo.

7
00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:19,260
It makes Earth's
magnetic field.

8
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:21,750
Freeze it, and
the field fades.

9
00:00:22,130 --> 00:00:24,710
Compasses
lose north.

10
00:00:24,710 --> 00:00:27,440
Migrating birds and
salmon lose a guide.

11
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:29,880
The polar
lights fade,

12
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:32,480
and over millions of
years the solar wind

13
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:34,740
could strip some
of our air away,

14
00:00:34,740 --> 00:00:36,910
as it did on Mars.

15
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:38,960
Yet volcanoes
and drifting

16
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:40,800
plates keep going.

17
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:43,890
They run mainly on the
mantle's own heat.

18
00:00:44,260 --> 00:00:45,680
Our core is
freezing,

19
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:49,360
but so slowly it'll
take billions of years.

20
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:52,570
Until then, liquid
iron shields us.
